SHA256 5e16dc4ce63fc9000b6e986c6c1bf6b0fe89d8bd10c27845d8f5e59afde748d3 .gnd-planning/maintenance/2026-11-21-evolve-constraint-sources/README.md
1: # Evolve and the unattended-growth sources, planned 2026-11-21
2: 
3: From [issue #218](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/218). A
4: maintenance pass, not a milestone. Nothing is changed yet.
5: 
6: ## The disagreement
7: 
8: `src/gnd/skills/gnd-model-from-text/references/unattended-growth.md` (lines 94
9: and 289) tells a growth host to write a new constraint's source as `sample` for
10: row evidence and `common-sense` for library evidence, always `proposed` and
11: `deontic`. `gnd evolve` admits a new constraint only as `llm-inferred` /
12: `proposed` / `deontic` or `user-supplied` / `confirmed` (rule D-12,
13: `src/gnd/evolve/service.py`, the branch ending at the "new or changed
14: constraints must be" refusal). A proposal written as the document says is
15: refused. Confirmed at `0f39c392` on 2026-11-21.
16: 
17: ## Ruling needed before the fix
18: 
19: | Choice | Effect |
20: |---|---|
21: | (a) Widen D-12 | `evolve` also admits `sample` and `common-sense` when `proposed` and `deontic`. The evidence basis stays in `source`, where `measure` and the provenance reports read it |
22: | (b) Change the document | The document says to write `llm-inferred` and keep the basis in `provenance.rationale_world_fact`. No code change |
23: 
24: Proposed: (a). The reporter's workaround is (b), and it hides the basis in
25: free text.
26: 
27: ## Done when
28: 
29: - The chosen side is changed, and a test builds a proposal exactly as the
30:   document describes and runs it through `gnd evolve`.
31: - For (a): `sample` / `common-sense` with `alethic` or `confirmed` still
32:   refuses, and the D-12 statement in the evolve reference is updated.
33: - The affected lane (`tests/test_evolve_*.py`, `tests/test_unattended_*.py`)
34:   and the structure and inventory guards pass. The issue gets a reply and is closed after the merge.
