SHA256 e09432f7549561d65a4c7dcad269249258b4e2af6008962e10b5e8bdecaf359f .gnd-planning/milestones/include-root-routes/notes/include-root-routes-plan.md
1: # Include-root routes · plan r1 (outline)
2: 
3: **Status: outline draft, 2026-11-21. Not reviewed and not approved.** This
4: plan covers [#217](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/217) and
5: item 1 of [#214](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/214). Items
6: 2–4 of #214 belong to [pyrel-rules-coverage](../../pyrel-rules-coverage/README.md).
7: Phases are outlines; none has a spec yet. `start-milestone` turns this outline
8: into the full plan and the IR1 draft spec, and the plan review runs then.
9: 
10: ## Goal and completion predicates
11: 
12: A version-5 root with includes reaches the routes that refuse it in 0.4.0,
13: through one recorded composition or flattening, never a silent fallback. Every
14: combination that stays unsupported refuses with a message naming it.
15: 
16: - **IR1.** `gnd judgments check` accepts an include root, temporal or not, and
17:   judges the same composed model `gnd check` evaluates. Receipts and the
18:   report bind the root and every include by digest.
19: - **IR2.** A temporal include root can be flattened into a
20:   `*.flat.orm.json` plus its `gnd-flattening/1` record, by `gnd extract` or a
21:   separate route (owner decision D1). Extraction itself may stay non-temporal;
22:   the refusal then names that.
23: - **IR3.** `gnd export pyrel`, with and without `--rules lqp`, accepts an
24:   include root by exporting its flattened model, and the output names the
25:   flattening record's digest. A changed include makes the export stale.
26: 
27: ## 0. Binding design rules
28: 
29: - **Projections are recorded.** As in the literature-interop plan: each
30:   flattening gets a record bound to the bytes it consumed.
31: - **Includes stay as they are.** Standalone-valid, no nesting, confined paths.
32:   This milestone opens routes; it does not relax include rules.
33: - **Same judgement, either route.** A non-temporal root judged directly (IR1)
34:   and judged through its flat model must give the same verdicts. A test pins it.
35: 
36: ## 1. Scope, sources and authority
37: 
38: | Source | Obligation | Phase |
39: |---|---|---|
40: | #217, "Problem" | `judgments.py:471` calls `guard_bytes(..., route="judgments")`. `require_non_temporal(model, "extract")` at `extract/service.py:191` and `extract/projection.py:319`. Confirmed at `0f39c392` on 2026-11-21 | IR1, IR2 |
41: | #217, "Request" | Either route. The reporter measured that a non-temporal root with reference populations already judges through the flat model | IR1, IR2 |
42: | #214, table row 5 and "What would unblock it" item 1 | `pyrel_rules.py:2415` `guard_bytes(..., route='pyrel_rules:2267')`; default export refuses `include:unsupported-route: export.pyrel` | IR3 |
43: | [literature-interop](../../literature-interop/README.md) LX1–LX2, closed | `gnd-flattening/1`, `model/flattening.py`, `witness/flattening.py` as shipped | IR2, IR3 |
44: 
45: Out of scope: temporal models in PyRel export (`export/emit.py:36` refuses
46: them) and anything #214 items 2–4 ask for.
47: 
48: ## 2–3. Contract sketch and dependencies
49: 
50: - **IR1** adapts `judgments.py` to load through the include composition the
51:   checker uses (`model/_includes.py`), instead of refusing the route.
52: - **IR2** adapts `model/flattening.py` and the extract bundle path
53:   (`extract/service.py:92-112`). Whether `flatten_model` already handles
54:   temporal rules is the first thing the spec confirms.
55: - **IR3** adapts `export/pyrel_rules.py` and `export/emit.py` to take the flat
56:   model and its record. It depends on IR2 only if D1 puts the flattening behind
57:   a new route.
58: 
59: IR1 and IR3 are independent. Start condition: none; `main` at `0f39c392`.
60: 
61: ## 4. Phases
62: 
63: | Phase | Outline criteria |
64: |---|---|
65: | IR1 | The #217 temporal root with two includes judges, exit 0. A non-temporal root gives identical verdicts directly and through its flat model. A changed include is refused as stale. Nested includes keep their refusal |
66: | IR2 | A temporal include root flattens; the record names each element's origin and the temporal rule survives. Extraction of a temporal model still refuses, with a message that names flattening as the route |
67: | IR3 | The interop fixture root (`python -m gnd.examples.literature.interop run`) exports in both modes, exit 0 in default mode. Under `--rules lqp` it gets past the include refusal and stops only at a #214 item 2–4 construct, named |
68: 
69: ## 5. Owner decisions and open questions
70: 
71: | ID | Question | Proposed |
72: |---|---|---|
73: | D1 | IR2: flattening through `gnd extract`, or a separate `gnd flatten` command | A separate command, so extraction keeps its non-temporal contract |
74: | D2 | Is IR2 needed once IR1 lands, given #217 asks for one of the two | Keep it: IR3 and PyRel users need a flat model of a temporal root too |
75: 
76: ## 6–9. Surfaces, risks, protocol, verification
77: 
78: - **Surfaces.** The representation-format includes section, the judgments
79:   reference and the PyRel export page each gain one sentence per new route.
80: - **Risks.** A direct judgment and a flat-model judgment could drift. Control:
81:   the parity test in §0.
82: - **Protocol.** `process-milestone` with the project rules in
83:   `.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`. Owner approval of the
84:   plan precedes IR1 code.
85: - **Verification.** Each spec names its focused lane from
86:   `test_public_v71_full_judgments.py`, `test_public_v71_judgment_successor_guards.py`,
87:   `test_extract_*.py`, `test_lx1_flattening.py`, `test_lx2_witness_flattening.py`,
88:   `test_pyrel_export*.py`, `test_pyrel_rules.py` and `test_mc1_model_includes.py`,
89:   plus the structure and inventory guards.
