SHA256 99bd2f9cd0de7b71ca7faff2443210b2d1bb7f26e0d6cf2df80bafb691fa042d .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/literature-host-interfaces-plan.md
1: # Literature host interfaces · plan r1 (outline)
2: 
3: **Status: outline draft, 2026-11-21. Not reviewed and not approved.** This
4: plan covers [#216](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/216) and
5: [#215](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/215). It also takes the
6: "host-scale reading and extraction" carryover from the
7: [literature-depth close](../../literature-depth/016-milestone-close.md).
8: Phases are outlines; none has a spec yet. `start-milestone` turns this outline
9: into the full plan and the LH1 draft spec, and the plan review runs then.
10: 
11: ## Goal and completion predicates
12: 
13: A host with its own corpus and its own model calls the two literature examples
14: as library functions instead of reimplementing them. The examples stay
15: examples: neither is promoted to stable CLI (both issues say so).
16: 
17: - **LH1.** `examples/literature/reading.py` exposes a public producer protocol:
18:   a call goes in, an outcome (`accepted`, `empty`, `refused`, and the existing
19:   others) comes out. `run()` takes a producer, a stop rule per document as well
20:   as the global one, the roster cap (today `ROSTER_LIMIT = 128`) and the byte
21:   budget (today `MAX_BUDGET = 1 << 20`). `SavedProducer` is one implementation
22:   of the protocol.
23: - **LH2.** `replay()` takes a caller-given input root and replays a live run
24:   with zero producer calls. The packaged fixture stays the default.
25: - **LH3.** `examples/literature/assertion_admission.py` takes the assertion
26:   entity (objectified fact type or entity type) by name. Its identity is that
27:   model's preferred uniqueness, not (work, passage). Optional roles are
28:   optional, with no `unspecified|none|n/a` sentinels. Every fact row attached
29:   to an admitted assertion is kept.
30: - **LH4.** Admissible polarity and attribution values are policy data, not the
31:   hard-coded `("asserts", "own-finding")`. A supported row that fails the
32:   policy gets its own disposition. `MAX_TARGETS` (today 1024) is a parameter.
33: 
34: ## 0. Binding design rules
35: 
36: - **Formats stay.** The stage-file, coverage-row and rebind formats are
37:   unchanged; #216 says they work as they are.
38: - **Fixture bytes stay.** The packaged runs and their recorded outputs are
39:   byte-identical with the defaults.
40: - **Example status stays.** Public here means documented and tested as the
41:   example's library surface, not a stable CLI.
42: 
43: ## 1. Scope, sources and authority
44: 
45: | Source | Obligation | Phase |
46: |---|---|---|
47: | #216 "Problem" | `reading.py:562` `run()` builds `SavedProducer(inputs.responses)` at `:566`; only private `_evaluate(..., producer=)` at `:445` takes another. Confirmed at `0f39c392` on 2026-11-21 | LH1 |
48: | #216 "Request" bullets 2–4 | Per-document stop rule; `ROSTER_LIMIT` `:41` and `MAX_BUDGET` `:40` as parameters; `replay()` at `:574` against a caller root | LH1, LH2 |
49: | #215 "Problem" | `assertion_admission.py:100` `project()`; sentinels `:30`; policy `:122`; `MAX_TARGETS` `:29` | LH3, LH4 |
50: | #215 measured shape | 98 % of claims share a passage; about half lack one actor and one object; 9 % have several conditions; 44 % carry a quantity | LH3 acceptance fixture |
51: | literature-depth close | Host-scale reading and extraction carryover | LH1, LH2 |
52: 
53: ## 2–3. Contract sketch and dependencies
54: 
55: - **LH1–LH2** adapt `reading.py` only; the stage loop already exists in
56:   `_evaluate`. LH2 needs LH1.
57: - **LH3–LH4** adapt `assertion_admission.py`; `gnd judgments check` stays the
58:   admitting command. LH4 needs LH3.
59: - The two pairs are independent and can run in parallel on separate branches.
60: - Start condition: none. Running it after include-root-routes lets LH3's
61:   fixture use an include root, which is the reporter's real setup.
62: 
63: ## 4. Phases
64: 
65: | Phase | Outline criteria |
66: |---|---|
67: | LH1 | A test producer drives all six stages through the public call. A per-document stop ends one document and not the others. A lowered cap and budget are honoured and recorded |
68: | LH2 | A live run with a test producer replays from its own folder with zero calls, byte-identical. A tampered input refuses |
69: | LH3 | A model with a multi-participant, multi-condition, quantity-bearing assertion and a passage shared by two assertions admits with every row intact. The packaged example still admits as before |
70: | LH4 | A policy file changes which rows admit. A supported row that fails the policy has a disposition distinct from an unsupported one |
71: 
72: ## 5. Owner decisions and open questions
73: 
74: | ID | Question | Proposed |
75: |---|---|---|
76: | D1 | Where the producer protocol lives: in `reading.py`, or a small shared module other examples can use | In `reading.py` until a second user appears |
77: | D2 | Name of the new LH4 disposition | `policy-refused`, beside the existing unsupported one |
78: 
79: ## 6–9. Surfaces, risks, protocol, verification
80: 
81: - **Surfaces.** The literature examples page and the literature tutorial each
82:   gain a "drive it from your host" section.
83: - **Risks.** A generic admission could admit rows the packaged example
84:   refused. Control: the packaged fixture's admitted set is pinned.
