1: # PyRel rules coverage · plan r1 (outline)
2: 
3: **Status: outline draft, 2026-11-21. Not reviewed and not approved.** This
4: plan covers items 2–4 of [#214](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/214).
5: Item 1 (include roots) belongs to [include-root-routes](../../include-root-routes/README.md)
6: IR3. Phases are outlines; none has a spec yet. `start-milestone` turns this
7: outline into the full plan and the RP1 draft spec, and the plan review runs then.
8: 
9: ## Goal and completion predicates
10: 
11: A model built with the literature-depth features exports as a PyRel rules
12: program for RelationalAI. Each construct is either enforced with `require`, or
13: left out by a recorded projection that the output names. No construct refuses
14: the whole program unless the owner rules it must.
15: 
16: - **RP1.** External uniqueness compiles to a `require` over the joined roles.
17:   The packaged `assertions/model.orm.yaml` exports.
18: - **RP2.** An anchored constraint is not enforced in the program. It is left
19:   out with a loss report, as `gnd export ossie` does, or carried as
20:   non-enforced metadata (owner decision D1). The rest of the model exports.
21: - **RP3.** `primitive: Number` either compiles, or refuses with a message that
22:   names the supported Integer or scaled-Decimal pattern (owner decision D2).
23: - **RP4.** The packaged flat literature model, `quantity_fixture/time.orm.yaml`
24:   and, once IR3 has landed, the interop root export under `--rules lqp`. Each
25:   program runs on the existing PyRel test harness.
26: 
27: ## 0. Binding design rules
28: 
29: - **No silent loss.** Whatever the program does not enforce is listed, by
30:   constraint id, in a report bound to the model digest.
31: - **Default export unchanged.** The default (checker) export already exits 0 on
32:   these models; its bytes stay the same.
33: - **Families stay registered.** New rule shapes register in
34:   `gnd.constraint_families.FAMILIES` and keep the common refusal order
35:   (AGENTS.md, model queries and family dispatch).
36: 
37: ## 1. Scope, sources and authority
38: 
39: | Source | Obligation | Phase |
40: |---|---|---|
41: | #214 item 2 | `pyrel_rules.py:855` "external uniqueness is a later phase of the rules programs". Confirmed at `0f39c392` on 2026-11-21 | RP1 |
42: | #214 item 3 | `pyrel_rules.py:864` and `:886` refuse family `'anchored'` | RP2 |
43: | #214 item 4 and its 6-line model | `pyrel_rules.py:190` "primitive 'Number' is not supported by the rules programs yet" | RP3 |
44: | #214 reproduction table | The six packaged-model cases are the acceptance cases | RP4 |
45: | Ossie export loss report (`ossie-loss-report.schema.json`) | The pattern RP2 follows if D1 picks a loss report | RP2 |
46: 
47: Out of scope: external frequency (`:596`, `:860`), exact averages (`:745`) and
48: temporal models in PyRel export. They keep their named refusals.
49: 
50: ## 2–3. Contract sketch and dependencies
51: 
52: All phases adapt `export/pyrel_rules.py` and the PyRel export reference.
53: RP1–RP3 are independent of one another. RP4 needs RP1–RP3, and IR3 for its
54: include-root case only. Start condition: none; it can run alongside
55: include-root-routes, but the two touch `pyrel_rules.py`, so they run one after
56: the other or on rebased branches, never as two writers at once.
57: 
58: ## 4. Phases
59: 
60: | Phase | Outline criteria |
61: |---|---|
62: | RP1 | `assertions/model.orm.yaml` exports under `--rules lqp`. A population with a duplicate (work, passage) pair fails the generated `require`; a population without one passes |
63: | RP2 | The flat literature model exports. Every anchored constraint appears in the report by id, and none appears in the program |
64: | RP3 | The #214 six-line model exports, or refuses with the D2 message. The quantity fixture's coefficient-and-scale pattern keeps exporting |
65: | RP4 | All six #214 cases reach exit 0, apart from any construct the owner ruled must refuse, which refuses by name |
66: 
67: ## 5. Owner decisions and open questions
68: 
69: | ID | Question | Proposed |
70: |---|---|---|
71: | D1 | RP2: skip anchored constraints with a loss report, or carry them as non-enforced metadata in the program | Loss report, the shape `gnd export ossie` already has |
72: | D2 | RP3: support `Number`, or document Integer / scaled Decimal as the route | Support it if RelationalAI has an exact numeric type; otherwise document |
73: 
74: ## 6–9. Surfaces, risks, protocol, verification
75: 
76: - **Surfaces.** The PyRel export page and the gnd-export skill list what the
77:   rules programs enforce and what they report as left out.
78: - **Risks.** A projected program could be read as full enforcement. Control:
79:   the loss report is printed and its count is in the exit summary.
80: - **Protocol.** `process-milestone` with the project rules in
81:   `.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`.
82: - **Verification.** Each spec names its focused lane from
83:   `test_pyrel_rules.py`, `test_pyrel_export.py` and
84:   `test_pyrel_export_boundaries.py`, plus the structure and inventory guards.
85:   Live RelationalAI runs are opt-in and named as such.

